<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell to 1,488.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell to 1,488.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, Nov 19, Reuter - The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,488 today from 1,504 on Nov 18, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route			   Index    Rate    Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1   US GULF/ARA	  1583    14.375    1649    14.969</p>
<p>   1a  TRANSATLANTIC RV   1423 10775.000    1446 10950.000</p>
<p>   2   US GULF/JAPAN	1706    24.375    1767    25.250</p>
<p>   2a  SKAW P/USG/F EAST  1777 14575.000    1817 14900.000</p>
<p>   3   NOPAC/JAPAN	  1717    15.844    1667    15.375</p>
<p>   3a  JAPAN-SK/NOPAC/RV  1616 12756.000    1633 12888.000</p>
<p>   6   HR OR HR-RB/JAPAN  1222    12.606    1222    12.606</p>
<p>   7   HR/ROTTERDAM	 1264     6.156    1264     6.156</p>
<p>   8   QLAND/ROTTERDAM    0907     9.969    0907     9.975</p>
<p>   9   FE/NOPAC/SKAW-P    0988  8644.000    0992  8675.000</p>
